Support the architectures Limine already ships UEFI binaries for

Zesko/limine-entry-tool merge request !63 (Sean Baker), merged into master on
2026-08-25 as e5540d97, not yet in a tagged release (latest: 1.37.1).
https://gitlab.com/Zesko/limine-entry-tool/-/merge_requests/63

Without it `limine-install` exits 0 on aarch64 ("The system is not x86_64.")
and `limine-entry-tool --add-uki` exits with an error, so an aarch64 install
builds its UKI and never gets a Limine entry.

RETIRE: delete this file and its prepare() line when the PKGBUILD's pkgver is
the first tagged release that contains e5540d97.

